# Build and Dependencies

Assignment 3 requires **four** build files: one per project plus one at the root that builds all three
(e18/b01). The skeleton root `CMakeLists.txt` already exists and adds the four subdirectories; the three
project files are TODO stubs.

## Root `CMakeLists.txt` (provided)

- C++20, `CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS ON`, `find_package(mp-units CONFIG REQUIRED)`.
- Defines `drone_warnings(target)` → `-Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic`. **Call it on every target we add.**
- Adds `common`, `Algorithm`, `MissionControl`, `Simulator`. Add `UserCommon` handling to the consumers,
  not as its own subdirectory — `UserCommon/` has no build file.
- `find_package(yaml-cpp)`, `find_package(TinyNPY CONFIG REQUIRED)`, `find_package(GTest CONFIG REQUIRED)`
  and `enable_testing()` are **not** there yet; add them when the code that needs them lands.

## Targets

| Target | Kind | Key properties |
|--------|------|----------------|
| `drone_common` / `common::common` | `INTERFACE` (provided) | exposes `common/include`, links `mp-units::mp-units` |
| Algorithm | `SHARED` | output name `Algorithm_207190406_209543255`, `PREFIX ""`, links `common::common` |
| MissionControl | `SHARED` | output name `MissionControl_207190406_209543255`, `PREFIX ""`, links `common::common`, exposes `common_mission_control/include` **PRIVATE** |
| Simulator | `EXECUTABLE` | output name `simulator_207190406_209543255`, links `common::common` + `${CMAKE_DL_LIBS}`, `ENABLE_EXPORTS ON` |

`ENABLE_EXPORTS ON` (i.e. `-Wl,--export-dynamic`) is mandatory: the plugins' registration objects resolve
`::common::MappingAlgorithmRegistration` / `::common::MissionControlRegistration` from the executable at
`dlopen` time. Without it every plugin fails to load. The skeleton's `Simulator/CMakeLists.txt` comment
says exactly this.

`PREFIX ""` suppresses CMake's `lib` prefix so the file is `Algorithm_<ids>.so`, not
`libAlgorithm_<ids>.so`.

The registration `.cpp` files belong to the Simulator target only — never link them into a plugin.

`UserCommon/` sources are added to each consuming target's source list plus an include directory. Expect
the same translation unit to be compiled into the executable and into a `.so`.

## Build

```bash
cmake --preset default          # Ninja, build/default, vcpkg toolchain from $VCPKG_ROOT
cmake --build --preset default
```

## Dependencies

`vcpkg.json` declares everything (e11 — no manual install steps in the README):

| Package | Used for |
|---------|----------|
| `mp-units` ≥ 2.3.0 | strong physical types; required by `common/Units.h` |
| `yaml-cpp` ≥ 0.9.0 | all config and composition YAML |
| `tinynpy` | `.npy` voxel map read/write |
| `gtest` | tests |

Do not add a dependency without checking the assignment rule: **standard C++ libraries only, or libraries
explicitly approved in the course forum**. If we use an approved external library, document its usage in
`README.md` (or `bonus.txt` if it is only for a bonus).

`.cw` files need no dependency — they are ClassicWorld visualization exports, not inputs
(`docs/open-questions.md`).

## Submission-time compatibility

The submission must build on Linux with **gcc 11.4+** and
`g++ -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic`. Verify in the devcontainer
(`.devcontainer/Dockerfile`, Ubuntu 24.04 + vcpkg) rather than trusting a local toolchain.

